	\item Validation plot: `output/validation\_distribution.png`.
\end{itemize}

\section{Reproducibility}
To reproduce the full pipeline from raw CSVs run the notebook `code\_improved.ipynb` in order.
Recommended commands (from the project root):
\begin{verbatim}
python -m pip install -r requirements.txt
jupyter nbconvert --to notebook --execute code_improved.ipynb --ExecutePreprocessor.timeout=600
\end{verbatim}
Or open the notebook in Jupyter / VS Code and run cells sequentially. Generated files will
appear under `bronze/`, `silver/`, `gold/`, and `output/`.

\section{Concluding Remarks}
The notebook implements a conservative, auditable pipeline: deterministic DQ checks,
explainable feature engineering, and an ensemble modeling approach that combines learned
predictions with peer-group ceilings and domain-aware adjustments. The `output/` CSV
contains the final per-outlet January 2026 potential estimates.

